   READ THE LAST TWO COLUMNS. This is the whole Clay problem in one table.

   P/EXH      : the ACTUAL flow. crosses BELOW 1 (min 0.764) -- the exhaust
                channel absorbs everything the object emits. enstrophy turns over.
                the ledger closes. NO BLOWUP.
   P_lock/EXH : the LOCKED flow -- the counterfactual in which the vorticity
                aligned with the stretching eigenvector, exactly the fixed point
                C1 forbids. It stays ABOVE 1 the entire run (min 3.071).
                Production would permanently outrun dissipation. The exhaust
                channel JAMS. That is blowup.

   The difference between the two rows is ONLY the alignment. Same fluid, same
   viscosity, same strain magnitudes. The geometry -- the wash -- is the entire
   margin between a flow that lives forever and a flow that ends.

